  "severity": "important",
  "description": "A flaw was found in util-linux's libmount. On Linux 6.15 and later, the X-mount.subdir option opens the subdirectory on a detached mount tree with open_tree(), which follows symlinks in intermediate path components, so a local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint.",
